{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug complete — landed & closed\n\n**Root cause (confirmed on current origin/main).** `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:record_mcp_backoff_failure()` unconditionally called `err deploy_failed \"component=mcp ...\"` (→ `err()` emits an `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR {...}` marker → `observability.sh` counts `^AUTODEPLOY_ERROR \\{` into `rebar/host:deploy_errors` → pages `rebar-autodeploy-errors`). It was invoked on the TWO documented-routine backoff paths: low-memory abort (after `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT`) and port-exhausted retire-cap (after `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP`). This contradicts `observability.sh` (~L284-291, L355), which documents those tokens as \"each kept out of AUTODEPLOY_ERROR so a routine retire-cap / memory abort never inflates deploy_errors\" (sustained case covered by dedicated `mcp_retire_cap`/`mcp_mem_abort` alarms). Internally-inconsistent plan → `plan_defect`; introduced by commit `2a0a4b19f2ab` (ticket 6964), which shipped both the contract and the violating code.\n\n**RED evidence.** New `test_port_exhausted_routine_backoff_does_not_inflate_deploy_errors` drove the real script with both blue/green MCP ports held and observed BOTH markers for one event — `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP {...}` AND `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR {\"reason\":\"deploy_failed\", ... fail#1 backoff=60s}` — reproducing the live 2026-08-30 incident. Failed for the right reason (routine path emitting deploy_failed) before the fix; GREEN after.\n\n**Fix.** Factored the backoff-timer bookkeeping (write `$MCP_BACKOFF_FILE` + prune, set throttle globals) out of the error emission into `schedule_mcp_backoff()` (no `err`). `record_mcp_backoff_failure()` now = `schedule_mcp_backoff` + `err deploy_failed` (genuine failures still page). Added `record_mcp_routine_backoff()` (schedule + log, NO `err`) and switched the two routine call sites to it. Genuine-failure paths (build/tag/run/unhealthy/handshake/flip) unchanged — still emit `deploy_failed`. Throttle preserved on all paths (AC #4). Net +24/-8 in the script; 2 new tests + helper.\n\n**Step-7 sibling census.** Over-cap retire-cap sweep already marker-only (correct); `config_manual` is a genuine operator-action error (correct to page); `deploy_errors` has a single producer (`err`). No other routine backoff path mis-emits `deploy_failed`. One observed-but-out-of-scope quirk noted: the store-missing path uses the review-bot recorder (`record_backoff_failure`, `$BACKOFF_FILE`) for an mcp failure — harmless (genuine failure, still pages), left unchanged.\n\n**Validation.** `make lint` (incl. shellcheck) + `make typecheck` clean locally. Gerrit change **2421** — `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1` (full CI matrix: macos + ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 pytest, lint+type-check, mutation, packaging all green) — **MERGED**. Closed with `--class=plan_defect --caused-by=6964-40bb-46c9-48a7`.\n\n**File-cluster serialization.** Landed FIRST and cleanly in the `autodeploy.sh` backoff-recording cluster (no textual conflict; Rebase-If-Necessary submitted server-side). The held-back sibling `prespinal-gem-kinkajou` (dbf0) can now rebase onto this. Overlap-flagged `e1d9` (handshake gate) was already in origin/main and edits disjoint lines — no dependency added.\n\n**Residual / deploy-window live verification.** The end-to-end alarm behavior (a real landing burst holding both MCP ports → `rebar-autodeploy-errors` stays quiet while `rebar-autodeploy-mcp-retire-cap` carries the sustained signal) can only be fully confirmed on a live deploy burst. The regression tests assert the observable marker contract that drives those metrics; recommend a spot-check of `deploy_errors` vs `mcp_retire_cap` on the next natural landing burst."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788075963025388001,"uuid":"bef28633-7529-44e7-aa97-697dfb517182"}